WEBVTT - global: decisions settled

NOTE
One cue per item, one second long, in the order the items were settled; the time is the order, not a clock. The identifier names the item; the text says what it is, when, and where it lives. A cue that is replaced is not deleted: a later cue says what replaced it.

wsn-only
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
2026-10-27 the author: we are only using Wirth syntax notation; everything else is deprecated. Every uppercase character is an IDENTIFIER = letter { letter } .

plan9-runtime
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.000
2026-10-27 the author: Plan 9 is the runtime for everything; ports are Plan 9 C programs, not awk (rc has no arithmetic; awk was my choice and is being removed).

numbers-are-literals
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.000
2026-10-28 the author: numbers are meaningless; a digit is an index, a folder name like 28 is its characters. Values are interpretations.

literal-and-reading
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A literal is what a script recomputes from a held witness; a reading is labelled as one. Who said what lives in ZIGUAROTH/SOURCES.md.

the-zeroth
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.000
YHWH, YAHWEH, GOD IS WORD, GOD OF WORD, WORD IS GOD, WORD OF GOD. Everything is compared to them first, independently (each file alone), then to each other, codependently (edges, faces, parity).

yhwh-yahweh-adonai
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.000
YHWH is YAHWEH with the vowels removed (consonant class, terms.mjs); ADONAI adds them: Leningrad Deut 9:26 points the Name with Adonai's vowels, and with Elohim's hiriq right after Adonai.

question-mark
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.000
? is the optional metacharacter: WSN [ ]. TEMPLATE = "GOD" [ " " SLOT ] " " "WORD" . SLOT = "IS" | "OF" .

codices-and-codex
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.000
_CODICES[0..3] = ALEPPO ROSETTA BEHISTUN LENINGRAD, each A-Z; a term renders to _CODICES/LLLL/&lt;path&gt;/&lt;term&gt;.wsn. _CODEX[0] is the braille and Aegean themselves (&lt;term&gt;), _CODEX[1] the same in WSN (&lt;term&gt;.wsn), at the literal path ending in the lowercase description.

absent-codex
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.000
A codex that lacks the term is optional whitespace: OPTWHITESPACE = { " " } . (as BNF written in WSN), not an undefined identifier.

code-trie
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.000
_CODE/U is an Aegean trie: separators 10100 10101 10102, each with the 45 Aegean signs; a code point is the path of its signs, highest place first, a zero digit an absent level. 28 is separate: the author's time scale. 05 was mine and is removed.

patricia-tries
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Every ZIGUAROTH/_* folder is a WSN Patricia trie: one production, folders as alternatives, single-child chains as one LITERAL; its sentences are exactly the leaf paths.

query-function
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.000
The query is Wirth's PL360 rotation of R0 R1 R2 by FLAG, then RESET(FLAG). Registers hold words the way Kernighan's B printed hello, world: a b c, four characters each; FLAG declares which constant b holds.

aegean-base
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Aegean numbers are decimal as a script. Sexagesimal (Babylonian) use is an overlay. OPEN: replace the decimal rendering, or add sexagesimal as a second declared view.

agent-numbering
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.000
2026-10-28 the author: the agent numbering is derived from colours and cameras. An agent keeps its hue (the dome's lights); its number is the hue's place in the order seen from the camera, a turn of 45 degrees keeping the order, a flip reversing it (agent-commons.js pov and flip). Seen from turn 0 clockwise: METATRON 1 SOLOMON 2 SOLON 3 ASABIYAH 4 ENOCH 5 SPEAKER 6 GENESIS 7; OBSERVER, the camera, has no hue. The canon manifest's fano-points are not the numbering.

cue-length
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.000
2026-10-28 the author: the cue length is the animation frame. A cue is one frame; its second is the frame, not a clock; how long a frame lasts is the renderer's.

submodules
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.000
2026-10-28 the author: boxedPINE's proofs/ (github omi-axioms) and types/ (github omi-types) are submodules, on main; the author asked Claude to manage them. A change is committed and pushed inside the submodule first, then its commit recorded in boxedPINE (git add types). AGENTS.md says how.

haskell-normalizer
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.000
2026-10-28 the author: "the haskell is like a normalizer now of the wirth notation". OMI.WSN's render is the normal form: Plan 9 writes WSN in it (zaudit), and render (parse text) == text is the check.

one-import
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.000
2026-10-28: OMI.Types carries every type exported in types/src/OMI (99). The three distinct Bools and Lisp's DecisionTable come as FanoBool, LispBool, RelationBool, LispDecisionTable.

omi-files-port
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.000
2026-10-28 the author: port boxed/omi-files to Plan 9 and remove each once finished. Settled: the contracts first (goldens and negatives to WSN, checked by zlazy and OMI.WSN), implementations project by project (the C projects port; TypeScript, Python, Emacs Lisp and Scheme have no Plan 9 runtime and would be rewrites). A folder is removed only when its work is on GitHub, another working copy exists, and its port is verified.

turn-and-exchange
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.000
2026-10-28 the author: stepd stays PL360 (IS and OF only), because the exchange is the observer or agent operation, not the turn. The turn is the even half of the three names' six orderings; an exchange of two registers is the other half and belongs to whoever interjects. Nothing exchanges stepd's registers yet; agentd's POST writes the floor's agent states, not stepd.

claims-and-provenance
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.000
2026-10-28 the author: "they are claims and proofs that we made which is why we keep provenance and compile findings to ZIGUAROTH when done for public scrutiny, we arent asking anyone to trust we did all the work they can follow all our steps and believe or modify the beliefs how they want, we have the unit test and WSN notation and even Haskell and Coq."

with-or-without-ziguaroth
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.000
2026-10-28 the author: "Once we build everything and can check everything we can compile a build with or without ZIGUAROTH from our Plan 9 ports." What the build takes from ZIGUAROTH today: pack.sh copies _CATALOG's YAML into run/catalog (read by catalog.rc, conv.rc, tries.rc), and witness.py reads each figure's name from _CATALOG. The z*.c checks, in/* and wsn/* build without it. The choice waits until everything is built.

literal-codepoints
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
2026-10-28 the author: "we removed physics from this and made it literal constant of code points or code point sequences for strict logic checking."

pixelate-proof
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.000
2026-10-28 the author: "If we cant build the logic proof and reason for doing something from established rules or proof then we have to figure it out but the PIXELATE proof is the ability to change a svg from the margins. I cant code so every factor that I am leaning on was derived from a proof of concept but since i cant code i couldnt maintain it which is why there is an overburden of projects and documents." The proof is boxedPINE space/src/border.ts and trace.ts (space.test.ts, The border and The trace), now also PLAN9/src/zborder.c (border.rc).

foundation
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.000
2026-10-28 the author: "that's the literal FOUNDATION everything is built on", boxed/omi-files/atomic-kernel, and the reduction question the author sent whenever an AI pushed back on a term: "What structure can be removed while the same canonical unfold / replay / projection still results? ... There was one design decision. The delta law: rotl(x,1) XOR rotl(x,3) XOR rotr(x,2) XOR C. Four choices inside that: rotations (not shifts, so no bits are lost), XOR (reversible), a constant (breaks the zero fixed point), mask to width (keeps state bounded). That is the entire design. Everything else was computed by the math ... Nobody chose 73." What the foundation holds: coq/AtomicKernelCoq.v defines the law at any width n with C the byte 0x1D repeated to the width (0x1D1D at 16 bits) and proves delta and replay deterministic; crystal.py adds B = [0,1,3,6,9,8,6,3], W = 36, position read as divmod(position, 36). Checked beside it: 10^8 - 1 = 3^2 x 11 x 73 x 101 x 137, so 73 is the smallest prime of decimal period 8 (core.test.ts: period(10, 73) = 8), B is its digits and sums to 36; every state returns within 8 steps whatever C is (zgnomon; Coq's Delta16HasExactPeriodEight.v proves period exactly 8 for 0x001D); under 0x1D1D zero is not fixed, while 8 other states are (I-195, gnomon-eight).
